<Layout title="Privacy Policy | Ultimate Bench" description="Implementation-specific information about Ultimate Bench browser storage, advertising consent, hosting, and contact data.">
<main class="content-page" style="--page-accent:#38bdf8;--page-accent-rgb:56,189,248"><header class="page-heading"><span class="page-kicker">Implementation-specific policy</span><h1>Privacy Policy</h1><p>What this static site stores, when advertising code loads, and how to make a privacy request.</p></header><article class="content-card"><p><strong>Effective date:</strong> July 28, 2026</p><p>This policy describes the current implementation of Ultimate Bench as of the effective date.</p>
<h2>Information handled by the site</h2><p>Ultimate Bench has no accounts and no first-party analytics implementation. The static site does not send leaderboard or arcade activity to an Ultimate Bench application server.</p><p>If you email <a href="mailto:ultimatebench.contact@gmail.com">ultimatebench.contact@gmail.com</a>, the operator and the email provider receive the address, message, attachments, and correspondence metadata you choose to provide. Retention depends on the operator’s mailbox practices; no fixed period is documented.</p>
<h2>Browser storage</h2><p>The site uses these first-party <code>localStorage</code> entries:</p><ul><li><code>ultimate_bench_cookie_consent</code>: whether advertising consent was accepted or rejected;</li><li><code>ai_arcade_scores</code>: local arcade high scores;</li><li><code>adventure_save</code>: local progress, selected character information, inventory, and achievements for the arcade adventure.</li></ul><p>The Arcade curiosity control uses the <code>ub-fact</code> <code>sessionStorage</code> key to remember which local fact to show next during the browser session.</p><p>These values remain in the browser until site code replaces them or the visitor clears site data. They are not transmitted to Ultimate Bench by the repository’s code. The current production interface does not store pet data or create first-party cookies.</p>
<h2>Google AdSense</h2><p>Google AdSense is the only advertising service configured. Its script is not requested until the visitor grants advertising consent. If granted, Google may use cookies or similar technologies and receive technical request information such as an IP address and browser/device information under Google’s own policies. Rejecting non-essential storage leaves the script unloaded. Visitors can reopen <strong>Cookie preferences</strong> on any page and change the choice; withdrawing consent prevents future loading by this site but does not itself delete data already stored by Google, so browser controls may also be needed.</p><p><a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy">Google Privacy Policy</a> · <a href="https://myadcenter.google.com/">Google ad controls</a></p>
<h2>Hosting and fonts</h2><p>The site is configured for deployment on Vercel. Requests necessarily reach the hosting provider, which may process request and security logs under its own configuration and policy. This repository does not establish which logs are enabled or their retention, so this policy does not claim a specific log inventory or period. Pages also request fonts from Google Fonts, which receives the network information required to serve those files.</p>
<h2>Recipients and choices</h2><p>Depending on the visitor’s actions, recipients can include Vercel as host, Google for fonts, Google AdSense after consent, and Google’s email service when a message is sent to the project address. No other analytics or advertising recipient is configured in the repository.</p><p>Clear the site’s browser data to remove consent, high scores, and saved adventure data. Use the Cookie preferences control to change advertising consent.</p>
<h2>Privacy requests and corrections</h2><p>For privacy questions, correction requests, or result disputes, email <a href="mailto:ultimatebench.contact@gmail.com">ultimatebench.contact@gmail.com</a>. Do not send sensitive information unless it is necessary for the request.</p>
</article></main></Layout>
